WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.893 --> 00:00:10.460
Rachel Okafor: You know, Morning Carol. How's the weather treating you up in Hartford?

2
00:00:11.951 --> 00:00:17.766
Carol Bennett: Oh, you know. Fifty-two and drizzling. I'll take it over the snow that's coming.

3
00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:28.035
Rachel Okafor: Ha, fair. So I've got um, the QBR deck up. Want to start with volumes, or do you want to just talk?

4
00:00:28.597 --> 00:00:36.269
Carol Bennett: Let's just talk. Uh, the deck stuff I can read later. Honestly the thing on my mind is the QM rollout.

5
00:00:37.422 --> 00:00:40.110
Rachel Okafor: So, okay. Where are you sitting on seats?

6
00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:53.260
Carol Bennett: Um, Seventy-one of the hundred and thirty licensed, so we're behind where I wanted. Denise has been out since the the end of August, and she was running the live trainings for the Hartford floor.

7
00:00:53.575 --> 00:00:56.797
Rachel Okafor: Right, you mentioned that. Is she back yet?

8
00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:08.407
Carol Bennett: Back next Monday, so I'm hoping we finish the remaining fifty-nine by end of month. And the scoring's been fine, people are getting used to it.

9
00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:12.610
Rachel Okafor: Good. Anything else in the platform giving you trouble?

10
00:01:13.193 --> 00:01:18.644
Carol Bennett: No, that part's okay. The thing I keep running into is the scorecards themselves.

11
00:01:19.238 --> 00:01:20.500
Rachel Okafor: Tell me more.

12
00:01:21.193 --> 00:01:33.690
Carol Bennett: So we're scoring a Medicare Advantage call differently than a P&C quote call, obviously. Right now I'm working inside the criteria that are there, and it's a lot of bending.

13
00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:37.856
Carol Bennett: I want to be able to build my own criteria.

14
00:01:38.651 --> 00:01:40.701
Rachel Okafor: Like define new questions from scratch?

15
00:01:41.221 --> 00:01:49.045
Carol Bennett: Yeah, and attach them to the call type, so a MA call gets the MA set and a P&C call doesn't.

16
00:01:49.045 --> 00:01:50.908
Carol Bennett: And let me weight things.

17
00:01:51.999 --> 00:01:55.811
Rachel Okafor: Weighting meaning some criteria count more toward the score?

18
00:01:56.345 --> 00:02:04.555
Carol Bennett: Exactly. Right now if an agent um, reads the required disclosure language, that's the same as them saying the greeting. Those aren't the same thing.

19
00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:08.802
Rachel Okafor: Okay, that's clear. Is it the disclosure piece that's most uh, urgent?

20
00:02:09.821 --> 00:02:19.965
Carol Bennett: It's the one that keeps me up. Um, I need to verify the exact required language verbatim, and I don't want to fold that into a generic criteria and hope.

21
00:02:20.995 --> 00:02:29.697
Rachel Okafor: Got it. Let me write this down so I bring it back right. Custom criteria, so, call-type-specific um, scoring, weighting, and the disclosure check.

22
00:02:30.066 --> 00:02:35.004
Carol Bennett: That's it. I'm not asking for it tomorrow, I just want it on the radar.

23
00:02:36.334 --> 00:02:42.287
Rachel Okafor: I'll take it to the QM product folks and see what's possible. No promises on timing.

24
00:02:42.682 --> 00:02:43.753
Carol Bennett: Fine by me.

25
00:02:45.167 --> 00:03:03.206
Rachel Okafor: Okay, quickly on the numbers. September was about 41,200 calls across the network, up maybe four percent from August. Google Ads conversions still flowing through with the GCLID matching, Salesforce is writing the call records the way your ops team wanted.

26
00:03:04.509 --> 00:03:12.137
Carol Bennett: Good. PreSense screen pops have been solid for the Genesys agents, the journey info shows up before they answer. No complaints there.

27
00:03:12.421 --> 00:03:17.911
Rachel Okafor: Glad to hear it. Uh, Anything you need from me before the next one?

28
00:03:18.942 --> 00:03:23.945
Carol Bennett: Just the scorecard thing. And say hi to your dog for me.

29
00:03:24.626 --> 00:03:27.918
Rachel Okafor: Like, Ha, will do. I'll send notes by Wednesday.

30
00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:30.797
Carol Bennett: Sounds good. Talk soon.
